  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Locked the Rustaveli lot booth. Home.
    - Resident. Papers in my left pocket.
    - Done for the night. Going home.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Lot closed. Nowhere else to be.
    - Sorted my registration at the district office.
    - Back to the block. Nothing to do.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home. Same as always.
    - Home before the evening deadline.
    - They shut the lot. I walk home.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Taking my wife to the anniversary opera.
    - Football training. Midfield on Sundays.
    - New in town. Seeking parking attendant work.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Lot's still open. Back to work.
    - Fetching my wife from her sister's.
    - Collecting my student stipend.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Starting nights. The lot just reopened.
    - Wife sent me for bread. She worries.
    - Registering for service. Just turned eighteen.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Papers. Here. Long shift. Three months through this checkpoint. Look it up.
    - Twenty-two years at that lot. Not once have I been late checking in.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - The lot is closed now. Just going home. I keep my head down.
    - My joints are bad in this kind of weather. Or whatever this is.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Just let me through. I have nowhere to be, and I'd like to get there.
    - I am not afraid of you, officer. I am just tired.
