  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b8a5a27c7b20729498d233b872b276b0, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The lot on Rustaveli. Logged the last car, locked the booth. Going home.
    midDaysAnswer: The district office. Sorting my registration. Lot's closed, so I have the time.
    finalDaysAnswer: Walked past the lot. Chain on the gate. Then here. Where else.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The lot by the train station. Six years there now.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Work. The lot is open. Full from morning, busy all day.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My sister-in-law's flat. My wife and I stay with her now.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My knee. It acts up this time of year. Nothing serious.
    midDaysAnswer: Joints are bad in this weather. Or whatever this is. No sleep.
    finalDaysAnswer: Some pressure in the chest. Probably nothing. I am sixty-eight.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing. Knees of a young man. I stand all day, no chair.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No. I sleep like a stone. Weather never bothered my joints.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing. Fit as a soldier. I only just turned fifty.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Twenty-two years at that lot and not one car stolen. Think about that.
    - This line moves slower than the lot on New Year's Eve.
    midDays:
    - The lot is empty now. Strangest thing I have seen. Stranger than this.
    - My wife would have hated all of this. Too much commotion.
    finalDays:
    - Twenty-two years, and they close the lot without even telling me.
    - I have a routine. It helps when nothing makes sense anymore.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 4827361
